=== Climate ===
Ehime Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate (Köppen ''Am''), characterised by warm temperatures year-round, heavy rainfall, and a pronounced wet season from May through October. The Katsuran Sea provides a moderating maritime influence on the coastal climate, while the interior highlands experience slightly cooler temperatures and higher rainfall due to orographic lift from the Shendan monsoon.

Ehime is one of the wettest prefectures on Ishijima, with the interior valleys receiving over 3,800 mm of precipitation annually—the result of moist monsoon air being forced upward by the Ehime Hills and the Oshi Highlands. The heavy rainfall supports the dense tropical forests of the interior and the lush kabosu and kiwi orchards that define the prefecture's agricultural landscape, but it also creates challenging conditions for construction and infrastructure maintenance.

